      "text": "```\nTHE ORIGINAL POSITION (Rawls 1971)\n====================================="
    },
    {
      "id": "05-RAWLS.md#006",
      "path": [
        "05-RAWLS.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:ethics:05-rawls, git-history:ethics:05-rawls]",
        "canonical_path": "ethics/05-RAWLS.md",
        "concepts": "[rawls]",
        "current_path": "ethics/05-RAWLS.md",
        "id": "maxim:ethics:rawls",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "ethics",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[rawls]",
        "section": "ethics",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Rawls: A Theory of Justice",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "WHAT IT IS:\n  A hypothetical thought experiment, not an actual historical state.\n  A device of representation: what principles would persons choose\n  if they were choosing from behind a veil of ignorance about\n  their own position in society?"
    },
    {
      "id": "05-RAWLS.md#007",
      "path": [
        "05-RAWLS.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:ethics:05-rawls, git-history:ethics:05-rawls]",
        "canonical_path": "ethics/05-RAWLS.md",
        "concepts": "[rawls]",
        "current_path": "ethics/05-RAWLS.md",
        "id": "maxim:ethics:rawls",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "ethics",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[rawls]",
        "section": "ethics",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Rawls: A Theory of Justice",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "WHAT THE VEIL CONCEALS:\n  - Social position: rich/poor, high/low status\n  - Natural talents: intelligence, strength, health\n  - Conception of the good: what you value and want\n  - Psychological profile: risk tolerance, envy, ambition\n  - Historical facts about one's society\n  - Generation: whether you're in the first, current, or future gen."
    },
    {
      "id": "05-RAWLS.md#008",
      "path": [
        "05-RAWLS.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:ethics:05-rawls, git-history:ethics:05-rawls]",
        "canonical_path": "ethics/05-RAWLS.md",
        "concepts": "[rawls]",
        "current_path": "ethics/05-RAWLS.md",
        "id": "maxim:ethics:rawls",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "ethics",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[rawls]",
        "section": "ethics",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Rawls: A Theory of Justice",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "WHAT IS KNOWN BEHIND THE VEIL:\n  - General facts of economics, psychology, sociology\n  - How institutions work\n  - The conditions that make justice necessary\n  - What primary goods are (things any rational person wants\n    regardless of their specific conception of the good:\n    liberties, opportunities, income/wealth, social bases of self-respect)"
    },
    {
      "id": "05-RAWLS.md#009",
      "path": [
        "05-RAWLS.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:ethics:05-rawls, git-history:ethics:05-rawls]",
        "canonical_path": "ethics/05-RAWLS.md",
        "concepts": "[rawls]",
        "current_path": "ethics/05-RAWLS.md",
        "id": "maxim:ethics:rawls",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "ethics",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[rawls]",
        "section": "ethics",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Rawls: A Theory of Justice",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "THE POINT:\n  The veil of ignorance ensures impartiality.\n  You can't choose principles that favor YOUR position\n  because you don't know your position.\n  You choose from behind genuine uncertainty.\n  This is a fairness constraint on the choice of principles."
    },
    {
      "id": "05-RAWLS.md#010",
      "path": [
        "05-RAWLS.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:ethics:05-rawls, git-history:ethics:05-rawls]",
        "canonical_path": "ethics/05-RAWLS.md",
        "concepts": "[rawls]",
        "current_path": "ethics/05-RAWLS.md",
        "id": "maxim:ethics:rawls",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "ethics",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[rawls]",
        "section": "ethics",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Rawls: A Theory of Justice",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "MIT TCS BRIDGE:\n  The original position is analogous to game theory under uncertainty.\n  Rawls' parties choose maximin (maximize the minimum payoff).\n  This is the correct strategy under uncertainty when:\n  - Outcomes matter enormously\n  - No rational basis for assigning probabilities\n  - Can't accept a really bad outcome\n  Rawls argues: justice involves all three conditions.\n```"
    }
